    description: 'Diploma to degree pathways in nursing and social work: up to 12 months credit into a Bachelor of Nursing or Bachelor of Social Work, assessed individually in writing.',
    text: 'Articulation pathways and partnerships. The learning you have done counts. Diploma of Nursing HLT54121: Credit transfer for identical or equivalent completed units; recognition of prior learning (RPL) assessed on evidence for other learning. No fixed number of months or units is promised. Eligible: CHC33021 Certificate III in Individual Support, CHC43015 Certificate IV in Ageing Support, HLT33115 Certificate III in Health Services Assistance,  Certificate IV in Allied Health Assistance, CHC43115 Disability-sector qualification Diploma of Community Services CHC52021: Unit-level credit transfer for identical or equivalent units, and evidence-based RPL. No fixed credit amount is promised. Eligible: CHC32015 Certificate III in Community Services, CHC42021 Certificate IV in Community Services, CHC43315 Certificate IV in Mental Health, CHC40421 Certificate IV in Youth Work, CHC43115 Certificate IV in Disability Support, CHC33021 Certificate III in Individual Support Bachelor of Nursing : Up to 12 months (8 units), with entry to second year subject to individual assessment. Credit is not automatic. Eligible: HLT54121 Diploma of Nursing Bachelor of Social Work : Up to 12 months, a maximum of 25% of the four-year degree, with entry to second year subject to assessment. Eligible: CHC52021 Diploma of Community Services, CHC52015 Diploma of Community Services Enquire Email a Pathway Advisor directly. Target first response: within 2 working days. Share your record Provide a verified USI transcript or academic record. Current students can share proof of enrolment for a conditional pre-assessment. Indicative credit Receive written indicative credit within 5 working days after your documents are verified. Apply Submit a formal application. Admission checks, entry and English / LLN requirements apply. Offer and acceptance The manual describes a 5 working day target for complete applications — a target, not an unconditional promise. Start well Priority orientation and a transition workshop help you settle into the new level of study. HCI Pathway Scholarship: 20 per cent off first-semester tuition fees.',
