    text: 'Bachelor of Nursing · AQF 7 · CRICOS 118071E Become the nurse people remember. Caring with passion, from your first day. An NMBA/TEQSA-accredited degree is taught the way nursing is practised: in small cohorts, hands-on in simulated wards, and on placement in city and regional hospitals and aged-care homes across Australia. Start in any of six intakes a year at four campuses, and graduate eligible to apply for registration as a Registered Nurse with AHPRA. Apply for the BNCompare three pathways Show me details for Duration 3 years full-time or part-time equivalent Units 24 units 19 theory + 5 placements Delivery Face-to-Face on campus + online Level AQF 7 Bachelor degree Campuses 4 cities Melbourne · Sydney · Perth · Brisbane 01Three ways in Where you start shapes the route, not the destination. Compare each pathway side by side: how it is structured, who it suits, and what is and is not promised. Pathway 1 · Direct entry School leavers, career changers and international applicants Bachelor of Nursing 3years full-time Registration is never automatic. Apply for the BNEnquire Pathway 2 · Enrolled Nurses Accredited AQF 5 Diploma AND current unrestricted NMBA/Ahpra EN registration Diploma of Nursing + Bachelor Up to 8units of credit, assessed individually Not yet an Enrolled Nurse? Start with IHNA. IHNA and IHM admissions are separate. EN registration, BN admission and credit are not guaranteed. Explore IHNA Diploma of NursingInternational Credit is decided case by case. Apply for the BNCredit & RPL Pathway 3 · Bachelor, then Master’s BN graduates who later want advanced study in leadership, research and education Bachelor, then Master of Nursing 3 + 2years, two separate courses Master’s fees are on the official Master’s page. Apply for the BNMaster of Nursing page Intake planner Pick your campus. Plan your first day. Course commencement dates by campus, from IHM planning timetables. These are first days of the course, not orientation dates or continuing semesters. VIC campus Melbourne 1 commencement date in 2026 WA campus Perth 1 commencement date in 2026 NSW campus Sydney 0 commencement dates in 2026 No scheduled dates No Sydney commencement dates are scheduled for 2026. QLD campus Brisbane 0 commencement dates in 2026 No scheduled dates No Brisbane commencement dates are scheduled for 2026. Dates are from planning timetables and subject to institutional confirmation and campus availability; applying early does not guarantee a place. 02The course Competence you can feel in your hands. The BN combines anatomy, pathophysiology and pharmacotherapeutics with the communication, ethics and clinical reasoning that make care safe. Blended learning keeps theory flexible; simulation and placement make it real. Person-centred, culturally safe care Including culturally appropriate nursing of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and global, cultural health care. Simulation laboratories Practise clinical skills in simulated educational labs before you meet patients on placement. Digital health Electronic health records, mHealth apps, virtual simulation and a dedicated Health Informatics unit. Rural, regional and remote A final-year unit on health and wellness beyond the cities, where placements may also take you. Clinical leadership Leadership, advocacy and a transition unit preparing you for the role of the Registered Nurse. Campuses Melbourne Sydney Perth Brisbane Course and intake availability can differ by campus. Please confirm your preferred campus and start date with IHM before applying. 03Professional experience Five placements. 800 hours. One rising arc. Placements are assessed against NMBA Registered Nurse Standards for Practice. They are normally in the state of your campus and may be in rural areas; travel and accommodation are generally at your own cost. PEP 1160h Year 1 · Sem 2 Introduction to clinical experience Interpersonal and communication skills, the nurse in a multidisciplinary team, caring for a healthy older pe',
