    path: '/english-language-proficiency-entry-requirements/',
    title: 'English Language Proficiency Entry Requirements',
    template: 'policy',
    description: 'IHM does not require applicants to provide evidence of English language if they are:',
    text: 'English Language Entry Requirements and Waivers Applicants from English-speaking countries: IHM does not require applicants to provide evidence of English language if they are: Citizens of English-speaking countries, OR Permanent Residents of English-speaking countries, OR Individuals who have resided in an English-speaking country for a minimum of TEN years and have completed secondary or tertiary education in an English-speaking country. Applicants are required to provide the following documents as evidence to support their application: Proof of citizenship or residency Copies of official academic transcripts (where applicable) Recognised English-Speaking Countries Antigua and Barbuda Australia Bahamas Barbados Belize Botswana Canada (excl Quebec) Cook Islands Dominica Fiji Gibraltar Ghana Grenada Guyana Jamaica Kenya Kiribati Lesotho Liberia Malawi Mauritius Micronesia Namibia New Zealand Nigeria Papua New Guinea Sierra Leone Singapore Solomon Islands South Africa Tanzania The Gambia Tonga Trinidad and Tobago Uganda Zambia Zimbabwe United States of America United Kingdom (incl Northern Ireland) and Republic of Ireland Applicants from Non-English-speaking countries English Language Proficiency Tests: IHM accepts the following English language tests, provided they were completed no more than two years before the intended start date and meet the minimum scores for the desired program. Applicants are required to provide copies of official Academic Transcripts as evidence. Course Wise English Language Requirements English Language Requirements Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing (GCAN)#, Master of Nursing# Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing (GCAN) Master of Nursing International English Language Testing System (IELTS) – Academic version Overall, 6.5 with no bands less than 6 Pearson Test of English (PTE) – Academic Overall, 59 with no band less than 52 Occupational English Test (OET) Nursing courses only For Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing (GCAN) & Master of Nursing: Minimum C+ in each component English for Academic Purposes (EAP) Minimum score of 70% # – For the Online-delivery/hybrid version of the course only, English Language Proficiency Test requirements do not apply if the applicant studied in a non-English speaking country and has completed a minimum of 5-years continuous education in English Language (including higher secondary and above levels). English Language Requirements Bachelor of Social Work International English Language Testing System (IELTS) – Academic version Bachelor of Social Work Overall, 7 with no bands less than 7 Pearson Test of English (PTE) – Academic Bachelor of Social Work Overall, 65 with no bands less than 65 General Exclusions to English Language General Exclusions to English Language Tests: In addition to the online-delivery courses marked in Table 2 above, IHM acknowledges the following as exclusions to English Language Tests. Applicants are required to provide the following documents as evidence: certified copies of official Academic Transcripts. an original statement or certificate (on official letterhead) issued by the Registrar, or equivalent, confirming that the sole language of instruction and assessment was in English. NOTE: Please refer to the accredited curriculum documentation as some courses have specific requirements. Where this is the case, the requirements in the accredited document apply.',
