    path: '/graduate-certificate-in-advanced-nursing/',
    title: 'Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing',
    template: 'landing',
    description: 'At IHM, we are dedicated to supporting your journey towards Australian Nursing registration.',
    text: 'Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing (12 Specialisations) Delivery Mode: Online Accreditation: TEQSA AQF Level: 08 Course Duration: Full Time: 26 weeksPart Time: 52 weeks Available for: Domestic Students International Students* 50% Scholarship for NCLEX training Apply Now Enquire Now Advance Your Nursing Career with the Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing The Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing (GCAN) is designed to meet the growing global demand for highly skilled registered nurses. This postgraduate program offers 12 specialised courses that enhance your clinical expertise, professional knowledge, and confidence in delivering high-quality patient care. Delivered entirely online, the program is taught by experienced nursing clinicians and academic experts. You’ll gain advanced insights into modern nursing practices, empowering you to provide responsive, specialised care to patients and their families. At IHM, our interactive online learning platform is tailored to fit the busy lives of working nurses. Flexible and engaging, it allows you to continue your professional development while balancing personal and family commitments. A fast track pathway to becoming a Registered Nurse in Australia GCAN is certified by TEQSA in Australia and allows overseas trained nurses to qualify for AHPRA registration and become a Registered Nurse (RN) in Australia after they have graduated It is ideal for international nurses who are already practising in specialised nursing roles and wish to deepen their knowledge and formalise their clinical skills *At IHM, we are dedicated to supporting your journey towards Australian Nursing registration. *This course does not lead to Direct Nursing Registration in Australia, Nurses aspiring to become Registered Nurses in Australia must need NMBA approved English Language Requirements and pass NCLEX & OSCE for Australia. Details about the Course Course Details Course Details This online course is for Registered Nurses who hold a Bachelor’s degree or equivalent qualification. Whether you’re working in a hospital, community health, aged care, or another clinical setting, this course supports your commitment to advancing your nursing practice. It is flexible enough to accommodate varying work schedules and personal responsibilities, making it ideal for busy professionals. International Nurses working in any country can enrol in this online course. This course can be your pathway to becoming a RN in Australia. Frequently Asked Questions Frequently Asked Questions 1. What are the admission requirements for the course? Have completed a Bachelor of Nursing degree or an equivalent qualification or 3 years Diploma of Nursing leading to Registration as a nurse in home country with a minimum of one year of work experience. Be an AHPRA registered nurse; or Be a registered nurse with the Nurses’ Board/Council from the country of origin or place of residence Must have English Language proficiency as evidenced by: English Language Requirements: Accepted Tests and Minimum Score Criteria You may be eligible for English Waiver English Language Entry Requirements and Waiver 2. Can I apply for the program if I have a nursing degree from a different country? If you have a current, valid nursing registration in your home country and meet the course’s admission requirements, you are qualified to apply for the program. 3. Can I pursue the program on a part-time basis? The course is intended for registered nurses who are already in practise, thus you will have the choice between studying full time or part time. 4. Are there any specific specialisations options within the program? The Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing does, in fact, offer a choice of 13 different areas of specialisation. Nurses have the choice to select their areas of speciality depending on their prior experience as well as their areas of interest. 5. What are the career prospects after completing the Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing? Ma',
