    path: '/library/assessment-guide/',
    title: 'Assessment Guide',
    template: 'library',
    description: 'Assessment guide is the major component IHM postgraduate courses. This includes variety of assessment forms including academic essays, discussions papers',
    text: 'Assessment Guide How to prepare and submit assessment: A Guide for IHM Students Assessment guide is the major component IHM postgraduate courses. This includes variety of assessment forms including academic essays, discussions papers, literature review papers, appraisals, reports, reflective journals and similarly many others. Students are expected to learn and apply the conventions of each assessment document and apply the current APA 7th style of referencing and formatting. All your assignments must support by evidence and sources properly cited with APA system. IHM assessment are designed to test your ability to synthesise into an original piece of work. The basic format of a paper or essay is an introduction, a body consisting of three to five main paragraphs and a conclusion. This format applies whether your paper is analytical essay, an argumentative essay or a literature review. This is one of two structural patterns you will see in published papers with the other being laboratory report format consisting of aim, method, results, discussion and conclusion. Both formats may be accompanied by an abstract at the beginning, which is a brief summary of the content. Download Guide',
