    path: '/meet-our-md/',
    title: 'Meet Our MD',
    template: 'about',
    description: 'Dr. Bijo is the Founder, Managing Director and CEO of IHM & HCI Australia. His demonstrated passion towards education, entrepreneurship and technology has',
    text: 'Founder & Managing Director Dr. Bijo Kunnumpurath Believe in the value of lifelong learning. Dr. Bijo is the Founder, Managing Director and CEO of IHM & HCI Australia. His demonstrated passion towards education, entrepreneurship and technology has shaped the vision of HCI Australia & IHM. Dr. Bijo Kunnumpurathu’s journey from humble beginnings in a small town in Kerala, India to becoming the visionary Founder, Managing Director, and CEO of HCI Australi is truly inspiring. His career began as an engineer and project manager in Malaysia, and over the past two decades in Australia, he has gained a profound understanding of the global healthcare landscape. Recognising the urgent need for skilled nurses, Dr. Bijo’s commitment to “Education for Employment” drives his mission to empower overseas nurses to address Australia’s critical shortage. Under Dr. Bijo’s dynamic leadership, IHM Australia has become a pioneer in career-focused healthcare training. His innovative programs are designed to meet industry demands, bringing transformative change and equipping individuals to excel in the challenging healthcare sector. Dr. Bijo’s hands-on approach to community engagement reflects his deep belief in education’s power to uplift lives and communities. Dr Bijo’s pursuit of a PhD in Good Governance in the Australian Private Education Sector from Swinburne University highlights his dedication to educational innovation. His recent recognition as an Advance HE Principal Fellow further establishes his leadership excellence and his significant role in shaping the educational landscape. As the Managing Director of HCI, Dr. Bijo oversees and manages the operational activities, systems, and policy implementation of the organisation. He is also a member of GAICD (Graduate of the Australian Institute of Company Directors). His community involvement demonstrates his commitment to making a global impact, with a leadership style characterised by excellence, innovation, and social responsibility. With a clear vision and a passion for positive change, Dr. Bijo continues to inspire and lead HCI Australia to new heights of success and achievement in education and beyond. Prospective students and those interested in connecting with Dr. Bijo can find inspiration in his story and his unwavering dedication to transforming lives through education. 042 368 2248 bijo@hcigroup.com.au bijokunnumpurath Get direct access to our CEO Dr. Bijo’s experience andexpertise on WhatsApp and take your healthcare career to the next level Chat With Our CEO Now! Dr. Bijo Kunnumpurath has dedicated himself to improve lives through health and wellness education, training and technology. Talk to Bijo NRI helpsNurses settle in Australia ~ A feature from the Indian Express In acknowledgment of Dr. Bijo Kunnumpurath’s distinctive contribution and achievement of considerable influence and advancement of learning and teaching in higher education through the promotion of professional standards, the Higher Education Academy of the United Kingdom awarded him a Principal Fellowship. Talk to Bijo Enhancing lives through education and training is what I strive for. Talk to Bijo With03Companies In over04Locations With400+Employees Our Organisations. HCI Australia IHNA Institute of Health and Nursing Australia (IHNA) Enhancing lives through healthcare training IHNA, is a healthcare training provider born out of the desire to enhance lives through training. As an Australian Registered Training Organization (RTO), IHNA is dedicated to giving the best learning experience for a successful and satisfying career in nursing, healthcare, education and community services. We’ve been committed to providing the best learning experience to over 14,000 students seeking a fulfilling career in nursing, health or community services since 2007. Our dedication towards caring originates from our work in healthcare, but it also extends to student welfare, administrative and instructional assistance. IHNA also goes ab',
