    text: 'Gerontology Nursing N8016 Dignity, expertise and leadership for later life. Registered nurses in aged care, rehabilitation and community settings caring for older people. Residential aged care Geriatric and rehab wards Home and community care Older people form a growing proportion of every community. This specialty expands your skills in chronic conditions, dementia and end-of-life care for people with complex needs as they age. It strengthens evidence-based, safe, ethical and professional practice that meets regulatory expectations, and helps you develop leadership while exploring the biological, psychological and social dimensions of ageing. Topics: Chronic conditions in older people Dementia care End-of-life care for ageing populations Scientific, psychological and social aspects of ageing Leadership and regulatory practice in aged care Parent award: Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing. Credential type: Proposed non-award micro-credential. Duration: 7 weeks (orientation week + 6 class weeks). Delivery: Fully online, 12 credit points at AQF Level 8. Fees: $3,000 per unit ($250 per credit point). Next intake: 8 March 2027, then July and November. Who can enrol: Domestic students and eligible non-student visa holders (proposed) Credit and pathway: N8016 Gerontology Nursing, N8017 Professional Reflection in Gerontology Nursing, N9001, Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing.',
