    text: 'Mental Health Nursing N8014 Presence, theory and practice, held together. Registered nurses supporting individual and community mental health across settings. Inpatient mental health Community mental health teams Consultation-liaison Rapid social change has created real challenges for individuals and communities, and every part of the health system needs nurses who can promote mental health. This specialty builds that capability. You will assess the nursing needs of people in a variety of clinical settings and develop a deeper understanding of mental health theory and how it shows up in day-to-day clinical practice. Topics: Mental health theory and clinical practice Assessing nursing needs across mental health settings Promoting individual and community mental health Role and scope of the mental health nurse Person-centred, culturally safe care Parent award: Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing. Credential type: Proposed non-award micro-credential. Duration: 7 weeks (orientation week + 6 class weeks). Delivery: Fully online, 12 credit points at AQF Level 8. Fees: $3,000 per unit ($250 per credit point). Next intake: 8 March 2027, then July and November. Who can enrol: Domestic students and eligible non-student visa holders (proposed) Credit and pathway: N8014 Mental Health Nursing, N8015 Professional Reflection in Mental Health Nursing, N9001, Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing.',
