    text: 'Neonatal Nursing N8010 The smallest patients, the most precise care. Registered nurses supporting sick newborns and their families in neonatal and special care settings. Neonatal intensive care Special care nurseries Maternity units Caring for newborns with significant medical issues calls for a skilled team with specialised expertise. This specialty focuses on supportive health care of newborns and on assisting the family through a frightening time. It is a highly technical area of practice centred on newborn assessment and nursing management, using clinical reasoning and evidence-based specialist knowledge. Topics: Newborn assessment and nursing management Preterm birth, congenital conditions and respiratory illness Birth trauma, peripartum hypoxia and metabolic disorders Supporting families of sick infants Evidence-based neonatal nursing strategies Parent award: Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing. Credential type: Proposed non-award micro-credential. Duration: 7 weeks (orientation week + 6 class weeks). Delivery: Fully online, 12 credit points at AQF Level 8. Fees: $3,000 per unit ($250 per credit point). Next intake: 8 March 2027, then July and November. Who can enrol: Domestic students and eligible non-student visa holders (proposed) Credit and pathway: N8010 Neonatal Nursing, N8011 Professional Reflection in Neonatal Nursing, N9001, Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing.',
