    text: 'Orthopaedic Nursing N8018 From trauma to recovery, every movement matters. Registered nurses in orthopaedic, trauma, rehabilitation and community settings. Orthopaedic wards Trauma units Rehabilitation Orthopaedic nursing focuses on preventing and treating musculoskeletal disorders and associated traumatic conditions. This specialty explores the impact of acute and chronic illness and the range of musculoskeletal dysfunction associated with trauma. It emphasises assessment and management strategies across adult and paediatric settings, using case studies, multimedia and discussion forums in a virtual classroom. Topics: Prevention and treatment of musculoskeletal disorders Musculoskeletal dysfunction associated with trauma Impact of acute and chronic illness Assessment and management in adult and paediatric settings Evidence-based orthopaedic nursing Parent award: Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing. Credential type: Proposed non-award micro-credential. Duration: 7 weeks (orientation week + 6 class weeks). Delivery: Fully online, 12 credit points at AQF Level 8. Fees: $3,000 per unit ($250 per credit point). Next intake: 8 March 2027, then July and November. Who can enrol: Domestic students and eligible non-student visa holders (proposed) Credit and pathway: N8018 Orthopaedics Nursing, N8019 Professional Reflection in Orthopaedics Nursing, N9001, Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing.',
