    description: 'Care that grows up alongside the child. Registered nurses caring for infants, children and adolescents in hospital and community settings.',
    text: 'Paediatric Nursing N8012 Care that grows up alongside the child. Registered nurses caring for infants, children and adolescents in hospital and community settings. Paediatric wards Children’s emergency Community child health Children and adolescents move quickly through physical, mental and social stages of development, and their nursing needs change with them. This specialty prepares nurses to work safely and professionally across paediatric settings. It places a strong focus on critical thinking, and on adapting new technology and treatments into safe, effective, high-quality nursing care for young people and their families. Topics: Developmental stages and paediatric nursing needs Safe, high-quality paediatric nursing interventions Critical thinking in paediatric practice Integrating new technology and treatments Family-centred communication Parent award: Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing. Credential type: Proposed non-award micro-credential. Duration: 7 weeks (orientation week + 6 class weeks). Delivery: Fully online, 12 credit points at AQF Level 8. Fees: $3,000 per unit ($250 per credit point). Next intake: 8 March 2027, then July and November. Who can enrol: Domestic students and eligible non-student visa holders (proposed) Credit and pathway: N8012 Paediatric Nursing, N8013 Professional Reflection in Paediatric Nursing, N9001, Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing.',
