    text: 'Palliative Care Nursing N8022 Comfort, dignity and courage at the end of life. Registered nurses caring for people with life-limiting conditions and their families. Palliative care units Oncology and haematology Community and aged care Nurses spend more time with people at the end of their lives than any other professional, and are uniquely placed to shape how palliative care is delivered. This specialty provides a systematic introduction to palliative care nursing concepts. Its person-centred approach supports safe, assured care in acute and palliative care units, haematology and oncology services, and aged care and community settings, using simulated case studies to build clinical reasoning. Topics: Palliative care nursing concepts Person-centred end-of-life care Caring for families through loss Palliative care across acute, oncology, aged and community settings Clinical reasoning through simulated case studies Parent award: Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing. Credential type: Proposed non-award micro-credential. Duration: 7 weeks (orientation week + 6 class weeks). Delivery: Fully online, 12 credit points at AQF Level 8. Fees: $3,000 per unit ($250 per credit point). Next intake: 8 March 2027, then July and November. Who can enrol: Domestic students and eligible non-student visa holders (proposed) Credit and pathway: N8022 Palliative Care Nursing, N8023 Professional Reflection in Palliative Care Nursing, N9001, Graduate Certificate in Advanced Nursing.',
