    path: '/research-strategy-ihm/',
    title: 'Research Strategy – IHM',
    template: 'research',
    description: 'Key initiatives include structured research mentoring, seed funding, workload recognition, and targeted support for peer-reviewed publications.',
    text: 'Research Strategy (2026-2030) IHM’s Research Strategy 2026–30 focuses on: Building a sustainable research culture Increasing high-quality publications and scholarly outputs Supporting early-career and teaching-focused academics Strengthening national and international collaborations Embedding research into teaching and learning Key initiatives include structured research mentoring, seed funding, workload recognition, and targeted support for peer-reviewed publications. Research Themes IHM’s research activities are organised around the following priority themes: Nursing Practice, Workforce, and Innovation Nursing Practice, Workforce, and Innovation Contemporary Nursing Practice and Clinical Excellence Nursing Workforce, Wellbeing, and Professional Identity Culturally Safe and Person-Centred Nursing Care Innovation and Digital Transformation in Nursing Aged Care and Chronic Disease Management Aged Care and Chronic Disease Management Healthy ageing and frailty Dementia care and chronic disease management Models of care and quality improvement in aged care Digital Health and Health Technology Digital Health and Health Technology Digital health interventions and telehealth Health informatics and data-driven decision-making Technology-enabled education and simulation Public Health and Health Systems Public Health and Health Systems Health equity and access to care Policy, leadership, and health service management Culturally responsive and community-based health research',
