    path: '/student-success-gcan/',
    title: 'Student Success (GCAN)',
    template: 'landing',
    description: 'The Student Success Programme has been established to provide support for GCAN students, with a specific focus on student’s personal success, including',
    text: 'Student Success Program for GCAN Upcoming events Ask your student support officers! Objective of the Programme The Student Success Programme has been established to provide support for GCAN students, with a specific focus on student’s personal success, including careers and nursing registration. Its core objective is to ensure that every student is: Engaged and supported throughout their studies. Confident and well-prepared for professional registration (e.g., AHPRA, OSCE, NCLEX). Career-ready, with the skills, networks, and opportunities to succeed in the healthcare workforce. Why this Programme is Important for You We understand that success is more than passing exams — it’s about feeling connected, supported, and future-ready. Through this program, you will benefit from: Tailored workshops focusing on career readiness. Guidance on AHPRA registration and transition to clinical practice. Opportunities to connect with employers, industry partners, and alumni networks. Your Role in the Programme This programme is for you and about you. We encourage you to: Participate actively in orientations, workshops, and support activities. Share your feedback so we can continuously improve the support we provide. Together, we can make sure that your time at IHM sets the foundation for a successful and fulfilling career. Upcoming events Keep an eye on your student inbox!',
